DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270104
DTSTAMP:20261116T000000Z
UID:a16c0d0eada559a0cf8e@tfl-closures
CATEGORIES:Part of the line closed
DESCRIPTION:🚧 Part of the line closed\n\nLiverpool Street (National Rai
 l) and Stratford to Romford\nDates as listed by TfL: Saturday 26 December 
 to Sunday 3 January 2027\nTfL's PDF lists this closure in more than one we
 ek\; it's shown here as one event.\n\nTfL live status (Planned Closure\, c
 hecked 20 November 2026): ELIZABETH LINE: Christmas Day\, 25 December\, an
 d Boxing Day\, 26 December\, no service throughout the network. Services r
 esume on Sunday 27 December to a revised Sunday timetable.\nTfL live statu
 s (Part Closure\, checked 20 November 2026): ELIZABETH LINE: From Sunday 2
 7 December until Sunday 3 January\, no service between Stratford and Romfo
 rd. The limited services to/from Liverpool Street National Rail station wi
 ll also not operate. There will also be no GREATER ANGLIA services between
  Liverpool Street and Shenfield. Replacement bus service C operates betwee
 n Stratford City Bus Station (for Stratford and Maryland) and Romford via 
 Forest Gate (Romford Road)\, Manor Park (Romford Road)\, Ilford\, Seven Ki
 ngs\, Goodmayes (High Road) and Chadwell Heath (Wangey Road). GREATER ANGL
 IA also operate connecting non-stop replacement bus services between Newbu
 ry Park (for Central line) and Shenfield / Ingatestone.\nTfL live status (
 Part Closure\, checked 20 November 2026): ELIZABETH LINE: Sunday 27 to Wed
 nesday 30 December\, no service between Paddington and Heathrow (all termi
 nals) / Reading. Use GWR services between Slough and Reading. There will a
 lso be no HEATHROW EXPRESS services\, or GWR services between Paddington a
 nd Slough / Greenford\, with some long distance services diverted to/from 
 Euston not serving Reading. Use PICCADILLY LINE services between Central L
 ondon and Heathrow\, and between Heathrow terminals. Replacement buses ope
 rate.\n\nSource: TfL planned track closures\, correct at Monday 16 Novembe
 r 2026. https://tfl.gov.uk/api/document/plannedtrackclosures.pdf?id=accc98
 cf-e761-47b3-a43b-3de08a097b8f&type=document\nPlans can change. Check befo
 re you travel: https://tfl.gov.uk/tube-dlr-overground/status/\nPowered by 
 TfL Open Data\nUnofficial calendar\, not produced or endorsed by Transport
  for London.
